# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/greatsword.clip: the greatsword family on both bodies (P2c wave 2, ACTIONS-2H; STYLE_P2 12,
# 25.8). The guard (angled up in front in both hands), hit 1 the overhead cleave (the blade over the back shoulder, the
# stance wide; the cleave at the ground line; the weight drags it on), hit 2 the waist-high sweep, hit 3 the finisher
# (the deep coil, overhead, the slam held, a deeper stance), the block, and the drawn walk / run (bow.clip's shipped legs
# with the guard). Timing at the hero's greatsword pace 1.18 (windup 82, strike 129, follow 153, finisher 330 ms).
# Written by ACTIONS-2H's tools/clips.py; `pauld=up` on the overhead wind-ups.
# (wave-2 fix round, ACTIONS r1, PLAN D81: no weapon pixel more than 2 rows below the sole row) hit 3's coil facing D at
# a202 (was a225, 4 rows under the soles) and facing U at a337 (was a292, 7 rows under), its follow facing U at a315 a
# row shallower (bob 1; was a292 at bob 2, 5 rows under). Both fists stay on the haft line (D81).
# (wave-2 fix round 2, ACTIONS; C3d) hit 3's overhead facing D is raised over the right shoulder (gs_2b, a045 behind): at
# gs_3b a090 both fists sat behind the helm and the blade stood out of its crown with nothing holding it (no hand pixel).
# (wave-2 fix round 3, ACTIONS; C3d) hit 1's windup peak facing U turns the head a pixel from the raised blade (head=-1,0):
# the helm's brim hid the fists on the hilt (24 lines); hit 2's windup peak facing R / L lifts the pauldrons with the raised
# arms (pauld=up), as hit 1's and hit 3's peaks already do.

